\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces The bit-coded construction on $a^{*}$ against \texttt  {"aaa"}. Every arrow between expressions points forward, and no $\mathit  {ri}_i$ is needed once its successor exists. The expression stays two nodes wide throughout while the bit-prefix grows by one $0$ per iteration. The dashed arrow is the one backward dependency that remains: $\mathit  {decode}$ must be given the original, un-annotated $r$ to know what shape the bits describe.}}{35}{figure.5.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single-pass}{{5.2}{35}{The bit-coded construction on $a^{*}$ against \texttt {"aaa"}. Every arrow between expressions points forward, and no $\mathit {ri}_i$ is needed once its successor exists. The expression stays two nodes wide throughout while the bit-prefix grows by one $0$ per iteration. The dashed arrow is the one backward dependency that remains: $\mathit {decode}$ must be given the original, un-annotated $r$ to know what shape the bits describe}{figure.5.2}{}}
